This patch is needed because Solaris home directories can be NFS-backed, and
SQLite WAL mode can fail during startup when it tries to mmap the `-shm` sidecar.

What it does:
- keeps WAL mode for Codex state databases on local Solaris filesystems
- detects NFS-backed SQLite homes with statvfs(2) and uses rollback journaling
- removes stale Solaris WAL sidecars when the WAL file is empty or absent
- converts existing WAL-marked NFS databases with a normal one-shot connection
- keeps WAL mode unchanged on other targets

Why it is needed:
- without it, Codex can fail at startup on Solaris NFS homes with
  `SQLITE_IOERR_SHMMAP` / SQLite extended error code 5386

